{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>You shall not go over [the boughs] again.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): do not search after the פארות, which are the branches, as it is said (Ezekiel 17): ״ותשלח פארות״." "<b>And by way of</b> the Midrash: לא תפאר אחריך — do not boast over the poor if you do them kindness and leave olives beneath the tree. The meaning is that it is fitting for a person to do kindness and not publicize it, in the manner of what is written (Proverbs 20): ״רב אדם יקרא איש חסדו ואיש אמונים מי ימצא״ — the explanation of the verse is that most people, each one of them, proclaims the kindness and goodness he does and does not conceal it, but a man of faithfulness who does kindness and does not publicize it, rather conceals it — who can find? And he called him 'a man of faithfulness' on account of what is said (ibid. 11): ״ונאמן רוח מכסה דבר״. And they further expounded: לא תפאר אחריך — do not take its glory from it; from here [we learn] that one leaves pe'ah in a tree. The Sages drew out the word תפאר from the language of תפארת, i.e., that the fruit is the glory of the tree, but Scripture designated the language of תפארת specifically for the fruit of the olive, which is not so for other fruits; and likewise elsewhere it designated for it הוד, which is the word of the prophet (Hosea 14): ״ויהי כזית הודו״. Behold, this belongs to the secret of language; and since oil, which is light, is called יצהר on account of light and תפארת and הוד — names of the supernal luminaries — therefore it was singled out with their names, for the glory of the Menorah, which includes all of them."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {0 "Source cites Ezekiel 17 without specifying the verse; the quotation ותשלח פארות is Ezekiel 17:6.", 1 "Source cites Hosea 14 without specifying the verse; the quotation ויהי כזית הודו is Hosea 14:7."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:50:58.073684203Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}